@@ -0,0 +1,105 @@
+# m165 a1h report: the bar's one More menu
+
+## Summary
+
+- The bar's Settings and Diagnostics icons are now one `⋯` menu (key `moreMenu`, tooltip `More`, 48 dp)
+  with Settings above Diagnostics, on every device that has a pad. "Show on this device" (no pad) keeps the plain
+  Diagnostics button and has no menu.
+- Tests first: `controller_app/test/more_menu_test.dart` (10 tests) was written before the lib change. Six of the
+  ten failed on the code as it was; the other four were passing, because the helpers fell back to the old buttons.
+- Test migration: the tests that tapped or sized the two buttons now use `openSettings` / `openDiagnostics`, which
+  go through the menu when the bar has one and fall back to the plain button when it has none.
+- No protocol, host or look change. `ModeMenuButton` and `BarModes` are unchanged.
+- Checks run: `tools/mine.sh` (format, analyze, touched tests) → OK, 13 files formatted, 2 packages analyzed,
+  110 controller_app tests and 1 party_host test OK. Also `flutter test` on the eleven named files (incl.
+  touch_targets_test.dart, which the brief's read list did not name but measures the bar's touch targets) →
+  +113 All tests passed.
+- Decisions:
+  1. `_SettingsButton` is replaced by `_MoreMenuButton` (MenuAnchor like `ModeMenuButton`). `_DiagnosticsButton` stays
+     for the no-pad case.
+  2. The More menu's `IconButton` uses `constraints` with `minWidth`/`minHeight` 48 dp (the named constant
+     `_moreMenuTouchDp`), so the touch target is 48 dp under every look.
+  3. The bar's Settings/Diagnostics keys are the menu items' keys `moreSettings` / `moreDiagnostics`.
+  4. `openSettings` and `openDiagnostics` keep working on screens with no bar menu (Connect), because about 20 test
+     files outside this job's allow list call `openSettings` and must not change.
+  5. `PhoneText.more = 'More'` added; the tests use the literal `'More'`, as the tests keep their literal texts.
+
+## Test values
+
+- `moreMenu` size: at least 48 x 48 dp, asserted by `tester.getSize` in the menu look at 852x393 (sunny and night) and
+  at 568x320 (menu look). The TV look at 568x320 is left out, as touch_targets_test.dart already does (the bar
+  overflows 12 px there; known, not this job's).
+- Palettes: sunny at `DateTime(2026, 11, 8, 12)`, night at `DateTime(2026, 11, 8, 22)` (the clock the test
+  harness uses for Auto).
+- `joined_view_test`: the full bar's `moreMenu` size is the compact bar's `moreMenu` size (`expect(..., more)`), and the
+  mode icon is at least as large as the More menu (width and height).
+- `host_mode_test`: the "Play on this phone" routes (full and compact bar) find one `moreMenu` and no Settings or
+  Diagnostics tooltip; "Show on this device" finds no `moreMenu` and keeps the plain Diagnostics tooltip.
+
+## Self-check (review-rules part A)
+
+1. Host setups: a TV host (`pumpApp` with `paired`, tv look), a phone on "Play on this phone" (`host_mode_test`
+   "the host route gets the full bar…" and the round's compact bar), a phone on "Show on this device"
+   (`more_menu_test` "Show on this device…", `host_mode_test` line ~179), a joined phone (`joined_view_test`), a peer
+   one build older: not touched by this change (no protocol change).
+2. Kept state: none added. The menu's open state lives in `MenuAnchor`; it closes when a pick happens (the item
+   handler runs; see Hand-over).
+3. Combinations: the pause menu, host away, player away, "Get ready", dropped link, results and leaving: the More
+   menu lives in the bar, which the existing `_TopBar` switches as before; no new state crosses them.
+   `host_mode_test` covers the round's compact bar and the picker's full bar.
+4. Stayed inside allow: yes, see the file list.
+5. Stopped rather than overstepped: `touch_targets_test.dart` was run, not edited (it is not in allow).
+6. Every look: menu and TV look, sunny and night, in `more_menu_test`; the 48 dp check runs at 852x393 and at
+   568x320 (menu look).
+
+## Files changed
+
+- `controller_app/lib/src/ui/controller_top_bar.dart`: `_SettingsButton` → `_MoreMenuButton` (MenuAnchor, Settings
+  above Diagnostics, 48 dp); the two bar builders use it when `controls` is true, `_DiagnosticsButton` otherwise.
+- `packages/party_host/lib/src/text/phone_text.dart`: `PhoneText.more = 'More'`.
+- `controller_app/test/more_menu_test.dart` (new): 10 tests (menu and TV look, sunny and night; 568x320 size; the
+  open-both-screens path; "Show on this device" with no menu).
+- `controller_app/test/support/pump_app.dart`: `openSettings` / `openDiagnostics` through the menu, with the
+  fallback to the plain button.
+- `controller_app/test/support/site_shots.dart`: `pictureIcons` takes `Icons.more_horiz` in place of the two icons;
+  the doc comment says so.
+- `controller_app/test/connection_test.dart`, `diagnostics_test.dart`, `haptics_test.dart`, `phone_fit_test.dart`:
+  tap Diagnostics through `openDiagnostics`.
+- `controller_app/test/host_mode_test.dart`, `host_title_bar_test.dart`, `joined_view_test.dart`: count and size the
+  `moreMenu` key instead of the two tooltips.
+- `controller_app/test/phone_look_test.dart`: the bar's icon colour is checked on `moreMenu` (its icon is
+  `Icons.more_horiz`).
+- `controller_app/test/host_own_player_test.dart`: unchanged (the plain Diagnostics button stays with no pad).
+
+## Hand-over
+
+- Harness question (not measured): in the widget harness a tap on an item of an open `MenuAnchor` does not reach the
+  item's `onPressed` (the menu closes, the handler does not run). A direct call of the handler works. `pump_app.dart`
+  calls the item's `onPressed` after the menu opens. The app's real taps are not measured here; a device check of the
+  More menu's Settings and Diagnostics items is needed.
+- Scratch files left in the repository root (untracked, mine): `mine.out`, `mine1.out`, `mm.out`, `named.out`. I could
+  not delete them (the Bash permission was denied). They are not in the Delete list because they are not in allow.
+- `more_menu_test.dart`'s 'Show on this device' test failed on the old code for an unmeasured reason (it needs the
+  puzzle load, which was missing until `setUpAll(loadPuzzles)` was added); the other nine tests fail or pass on the old
+  code as described under Summary.
+
+## Commit message — a draft
+
+Bar: one More menu for Settings and Diagnostics
+
+Settings and Diagnostics move from two icons into one ⋯ menu on the
+bar, on every device with a pad (owner round B-042 to B-044). The menu
+is 48 dp under both looks; Settings sits above Diagnostics. "Show on
+this device" has no pad, so it keeps the plain Diagnostics button.
+The tests that tapped or counted the two buttons open them through
+openSettings and openDiagnostics, which go through the menu.
+
+## Status row
+
+m165 a1h: the bar's Settings and Diagnostics are one More menu (done in controller_top_bar.dart, tests migrated,
+more_menu_test.dart added); open: device check of the menu's taps (widget harness does not deliver them) and the
+scratch files in the repo root.
+
+## Delete
+
